 $$\frac{B'}{1-\beta  B  - \frac{1}{2}  \sigma^2  B^2}=1$$ 
 $$\int \frac{dB}{1-\beta  B  - \frac{1}{2}  \sigma^2  B^2}=\int ds =s+c$$ 
 $$s+c=\frac{2}{\sqrt{\beta+2\sigma^2}}\tanh^{-1}\left(\frac{\sigma^2B+\beta}{\sqrt{\beta+2\sigma^2}} \right)$$ 
Inverting for  $B$  leads to :
 $$B=\frac{1}{\sigma^2}\left(\sqrt{\beta+2\sigma^2}\tanh\left(\frac{\sqrt{\beta+2\sigma^2}}{2}(s+c) \right)-\beta \right)$$ 
 $$B(s)=\frac{1}{\sigma^2}\left(\gamma\tanh\left(\gamma(s+c) \right)-\beta \right)$$ 
We cannot compare to the equation that you found because a constant of integration is missing into it. 
